# What UI jank is read from, beside the `frametimeline` source's per-frame deadlines: the demo's main
# thread and RenderThread, what they were doing inside each frame, and the garbage collector. Wanted by
# the jank scenario, whose metrics are frame percentiles, jank, main-thread blocking and GC time
# (https://github.com/ramesh130/perfettoagent/issues/6).
#
# Each atrace category is here for something those metrics read:
#   view     `Choreographer#doFrame` on the main thread and `DrawFrame` on the RenderThread, which are
#            `android_frames`, joined to the frame timeline by their vsync id; and `deliverInputEvent`,
#            inside which a tap's click handler runs
#   dalvik   ART's GC slices on the demo's `HeapTaskDaemon`, and its waits for one on other threads
#   binder_driver  binder transactions, so a main thread waiting on another process says which
# and `atrace_apps` adds the demo's own `Trace` sections: Compose's, AndroidX's and Media3's.
#
# Not `gfx`, for the reason the startup fragment gives: SurfaceFlinger's, most of a trace's slices, and
# nothing here reads it. The frames are the app's `view` slices and the `frametimeline` source.
# Not `am`, `wm` or `res` either: the demo is running before this trace starts and nothing is launched
# inside it, and no process is born in it, so neither are the task events the startup fragment names.
#
# The scheduler events are what `thread_state` is built from: whether the main thread was running,
# runnable, sleeping, or blocked in the kernel during a frame. `sched_blocked_reason` says why a thread
# blocked uninterruptibly. `compact_sched` packs the two busiest events, as the startup fragment does.
#
# ref: https://perfetto.dev/docs/data-sources/frametimeline
# ref: https://perfetto.dev/docs/data-sources/cpu-scheduling
# ref: https://perfetto.dev/docs/data-sources/atrace
# ref: https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/perfetto/+/refs/tags/v58.2/src/trace_processor/perfetto_sql/stdlib/android/frames/timeline.sql
# ref: https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/perfetto/+/refs/tags/v58.2/src/trace_processor/perfetto_sql/stdlib/android/garbage_collection.sql
data_sources {
  config {
    name: "linux.ftrace"
    ftrace_config {
      ftrace_events: "sched/sched_switch"
      ftrace_events: "sched/sched_waking"
      ftrace_events: "sched/sched_blocked_reason"
      ftrace_events: "sched/sched_process_exit"
      ftrace_events: "sched/sched_process_free"
      atrace_categories: "view"
      atrace_categories: "dalvik"
      atrace_categories: "binder_driver"
      atrace_apps: "@PACKAGE@"
      compact_sched {
        enabled: true
      }
    }
  }
}
